  "tutorHistory": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Explain this concept simply"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is the simplest way to picture **Current Electricity**:\n\n* **Voltage (V)** is the water pump pressure pushing charge.\n* **Current (I)** is the flow rate of water gallons per second.\n* **Resistance (R)** is pebbles and narrow pipes choking the flow.\n* **Internal Resistance (r)** is friction inside the water pump itself!\n\nWhen you ask the pump for maximum water, its own internal friction eats some pressure before the water ever leaves the spout. Does that visual click?"
    }
